      "id": "xpbd-finite-response-sum-overflow",
      "classification": "Existing /root/rig_identity conditional current source finding; newly assessed authored fixture context, zero new unique count.",
      "observation": "The source test decodes inverse-mass words, directly calls private resolve, then checks its returned count and exact encoded position/velocity words. In the separately displayed current VertexTriangle fixture window 1711\u20131832, all four inverse-mass words are 2139095039 (f32::MAX); the authored expected resolved count is 1 and each corrected position word matches the predicted position word. The presence of these expectations does not prove a test ran, product failure occurred, or identify the arithmetic cause of this particular case.",
      "relationship": "Earlier conditional finding traces a distinct symbolic finite-mass effective-response overflow. 059 q445 records individual finite/nonnegative mass validation; original rig ADD127 and 059 L12-921 independently read the full historical fixture. Exact causal equivalence and supported range need further source/policy reconciliation; no alias or count is assumed.",
      "future_repair_direction": "Decide supported physical inverse-mass and derived-response range, and reconsider whether an authored resolved-but-unchanged extreme-mass snapshot encodes intended behavior when addressing the existing finding. Preserve valid pinned and ordinary mass cases; no repair, fixture modification or test is performed now.",
